# UPGRADE_LOG — Ollama Max Evolution

## 2026-04-29: Phase 1 — Ollama Migration (llm_tools rewrite) ✅

### Commit: `71c0de2` on branch `upgrade/ollama-max-evolution`

**What changed:**
- Complete rewrite of `llm_tools/main.py` (393 → 583 lines)
- Added `httpx>=0.28.0` dependency to `pyproject.toml`
- Expanded test suite from 22 to 66 tests (all passing)

**New architecture:**
- Dual client system:
  - `_get_client()` → OpenAI client at `OLLAMA_URL/v1` (backward-compatible chat completions)
  - `_get_native()` → httpx client at `OLLAMA_URL` (native Ollama API: /api/chat, /api/embed, /api/tags, /api/show)
- Tier-based model routing via `_resolve_model(tier, model)`:
  - `fast` → `OLLAMA_FAST_MODEL` (default: nemotron-3-nano-4b)
  - `standard` → `OLLAMA_STANDARD_MODEL` (default: qwen3.5:9b)
  - `deep` → `OLLAMA_DEEP_MODEL` (default: devstral-2)
  - `auto` → standard (safe default)
- Cloud model detection: `_is_cloud_model()` identifies devstral-*, deepseek-v4-*, glm-5-*, gemini-3-* prefixes
  - Cloud models get 50k char input limits vs 12k for local models

